## Skill Learned
During this laboratory, I learned how to investigate a Linux cloud environment using command-line tools. I learned how to check CPU, memory, storage, networking, and operating system information.

I also improved my understanding of cloud infrastructure services. I learned how AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud provide similar infrastructure services under different names.

I also practiced using GitHub and Markdown to organize and document technical work.

## Challenges Encountered
One challenge was understanding the information returned by Linux commands. I needed to identify which values matched the laboratory requirements. I also needed to understand how Linux resources relate to cloud infrastructure concepts.

Another challenge involved organizing the required Markdown files and screenshots in GitHub. I needed to follow the correct folder structure and filenames.

I addressed these challenges by reviewing each command output and documenting the results in an organized way.
